ances formation; remote progress is rebuilt on authority reset while committed log history constrains future leaders through freshness and prefix checks. Pending configuration entries limit new proposals, and committed-but-unapplied work suppresses campaigning to avoid stale membership authority. RSM accepts legal configuration transitions then updates raft quorum membership. ReadIndex separately confirms current leadership only after current-term commitment, probes voting members and resolves a queued prefix; application and exact request context determine client completion. Old nonzero-term replies are filtered, pending read support is discarded on reset, and old log entries remain recoverable rather than being treated as current quorum proof.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-formation\",\n        \"B-authority\",\n        \"B-membership\",\n        \"B-read-admit\",\n        \"B-read-confirm\",\n        \"B-read-deliver\",\n        \"B-read-client\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-committed\",\n        \"F-pending-read\",\n        \"F-confirmed-read\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"S-term\",\n        \"S-formation\",\n        \"S-membership\",\n        \"S-rsm-config\",\n        \"S-read-consume\",\n        \"S-read-queue\",\n        \"S-read-response\",\n        \"S-client-batches\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"open_details\": [\n      \"Remote read-index queue-prefix response context and request correlation.\",\n      \"Read confirmation support spanning membership changes; legal schedules and retained confirmations need investigation.\",\n      \"Logdb crash atomicity, session replay and on-disk state-machine variants remain local unread details.\"\n    ],\n    \"core_gaps\": [],\n    \"status\": \"usable\",\n    \"rationale\": \"Representative formation and authority paths, their history/membership coupling and application boundaries are traced. Local questions and variants remain open; this is not coverage or correctness cer